/examples/*/.theokit/

# Test fixtures under tests/fixtures/repos/*/.theokit ARE tracked — a contract
# test reads `.theokit/rules/*.md` out of them. The exemption used to be
# asserted by the comment above and implemented nowhere: the bare `.theokit/`
# rule near the top of this file matches at any depth, so the fixture's rule
# files were ignored, existed only on machines where someone had run the suite,
# and the contract test failed in CI and in every fresh checkout while passing
# locally. Git cannot re-include a file whose parent DIRECTORY is excluded, so
# the directory chain has to be unexcluded first — hence two lines, not one.
!/packages/sdk/tests/fixtures/repos/*/.theokit/
!/packages/sdk/tests/fixtures/repos/*/.theokit/**
.gstack/

