BACKLOG.md
BACKLOG-ARCHIVE.md

# Stryker mutation testing — transient sandbox (a full copy of src/) + tool reports.
# Both are machine-generated per run. Left untracked they make the working tree dirty,
# which breaks the clean-tree pre-condition of cycle-release and cycle-code-quality;
# biome reads this file (biome.json vcs.useIgnoreFile) so this also stops the formatter
# from linting a generated copy of the source.
.stryker-tmp/
packages/*/reports/
reports/

# Scratch tree written by tools/check-doc-api-drift.mjs: ~48 probe files at the
# repo root, live only while it typechecks them. Both of its exits clean up, so
# what leaves them behind is the run being interrupted DURING the typecheck —
# the slow middle. Measured 2026-09-01: they survived, `git add -A` staged all
# 48, and Biome failed the commit on them. Ignoring the path is what makes an
# interrupted run merely slow instead of a defect in the next commit.
.api-drift-probe/

# tsup writes a transient bundled config next to tsup.config.ts
packages/*/tsup.config.bundled_*.mjs

# Stryker copies these into its sandbox and leaves them behind. They are not ignored by default, so
# a `git add -A` after any mutation run sweeps them in — and Biome then fails the repo-wide gate on
# a file nobody wrote. Observed twice on 2026-09-14, the second time blocking a commit.
stryker-setup-*.js
